import ../../../testing/driver.dl

set measurements to 0
function [measure a fresh layout] {a pointer:font} containing {C string:text} counting {integer:count}:
    globals:
        measurements
    execute:
        increment measurements
        return the test UI width of font containing text counting count

document fresh layout:
    paragraph "Body" containing "A measured paragraph" using no UI appearance
set instance to an instance of fresh layout
set driver to the value at (the test UI driver)
set driver's measure text to (the function named "measure a fresh layout $ containing $ counting $") as a pointer
set view to a UI view of (the address of instance) sized 500 by 400 using font "regular" with (the address of driver)
set measurements to 0
update the UI viewport in (the address of view)
update the UI viewport in (the address of view)
require condition (measurements = 0) reporting "An unchanged document was measured again before its first paint"
set the text of "Body" in (the address of instance) to "Changed text"
reflow the UI document in (the address of view)
set measurements to 0
update the UI viewport in (the address of view)
require condition (measurements = 0) reporting "An explicit reflow was repeated before painting"
set view's width to 280
update the UI viewport in (the address of view)
require condition (measurements > 0) reporting "A changed viewport did not invalidate layout"
set measurements to 0
update the UI viewport in (the address of view)
require condition (measurements = 0) reporting "A resized document was measured more than once"
set view's images changed to true
update the UI viewport in (the address of view)
require condition ((measurements > 0) and (view's images changed = false)) reporting "Image completion did not refresh layout"
close the address of view
close the address of instance
print line "Document layout tracks its own viewport, content and image freshness before painting."
